        <section class="mt-12 bg-white rounded-lg p-6 shadow-sm">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">About DWC Pipes</h2>
            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Double Wall Corrugated (DWC) pipes represent a modern,
                application-focused solution for subsurface drainage, sewerage and cable protection systems. By
                combining a smooth internal bore with an externally corrugated wall, DWC pipes offer the hydraulic
                advantages of low friction flow and the structural benefits of corrugated geometry. The corrugated
                outer profile imparts high flexural stiffness and crush resistance while allowing the pipe to remain
                lightweight and easy to handle. These characteristics make DWC pipes especially suitable for long
                runs in stormwater management, culverts, and protective conduits for utility cables where ground
                movement and settlement might otherwise compromise rigid pipe systems.</p>

            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Solanki Pipes manufactures DWC using carefully selected
                polyethylene (PE) formulations that balance toughness, environmental stress crack resistance and
                chemical stability. Our extrusion and corrugation processes are controlled for dimensional accuracy and
                consistent mechanical properties, ensuring predictable installation behaviour and reliable long-term
                performance. Jointing systems are engineered to provide watertight connections that resist soil
                ingress and groundwater infiltration, which helps maintain system hydraulics and reduces the risk of
                contamination. Because the pipes are lightweight, handling and transportation costs are reduced and
                installation times are faster this translates directly into lower project costs and reduced on-site
                labour requirements.</p>

            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">In design and specification, DWC pipes offer flexibility: a
                wide range of diameters, stiffness classes and accessory fittings allow engineers to size systems for
                the specific hydraulic demands and loadings of a site. They are compatible with conventional trench
                bedding as well as trenchless techniques such as slip-lining and directional drilling in select
                sizes. The material's resistance to corrosion and biological growth reduces maintenance needs and
                extends functional life compared to metal alternatives. For infrastructure owners, this means
                reduced lifecycle costs and improved reliability. At Solanki Pipes, every DWC product is subjected to
                stringent quality checks and testing to meet industry standards and customer specifications, ensuring
                consistent performance across diverse installation conditions.</p>

            <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Beyond technical performance, DWC systems contribute to
                sustainable construction practices. Lower material mass and easier installation reduce the carbon
                footprint of pipeline projects, and the longevity of PE materials reduces the frequency of replacements
                and associated environmental impacts. Whether for municipal drainage schemes, agricultural land
                drainage, industrial site work or utility protection, DWC pipes from Solanki Pipes are designed to
                deliver dependable service, straightforward installation and cost-effective lifecycle performance.</p>
        </section>

